# Data Dictionary — `heart_disease_processed.csv`

**Source file:** `data/processed/heart_disease_processed.csv`
**Produced by:** `data/processing/heart_disease_processing.ipynb`
**Source data:** merged UCI Heart Disease records from four sites — Cleveland (USA), Hungary, Switzerland, and VA Long Beach (USA)
**Rows:** 918 (one row per patient record)
**Columns:** 14
**Missing values:** none — all columns are fully populated after cleaning/imputation
**Duplicate rows:** none

---

## Column Reference

| # | Column | Type | Description | Valid Values / Range | Missing in Raw Data | Cleaning Applied |
|---|--------|------|--------------|------------------------|----------------------|-------------------|
| 1 | `country` | string | Site/country where the patient record was collected | `Cleveland (USA)`, `Hungary`, `Switzerland`, `VA Long Beach (USA)` | 0% | none needed |
| 2 | `age` | float | Patient age in years | 0–120 | 0% | out-of-range values would have been set to missing (none found) |
| 3 | `sex` | int | Patient biological sex | `0` = female, `1` = male | 0% | none needed |
| 4 | `cp` | int | Chest pain type | `1` = typical angina, `2` = atypical angina, `3` = non-anginal pain, `4` = asymptomatic | 0% | none needed |
| 5 | `trestbps` | float | Resting blood pressure on admission to hospital (mm Hg) | > 0, typically 80–200 | 6.4% + 1 illogical (`0`) | `0` treated as invalid → set to missing, then imputed with the per-country median |
| 6 | `chol` | float | Serum cholesterol (mg/dl) | > 0, typically 100–600 | 3.3% + 172 illogical (`0`) | `0` treated as invalid (a living patient cannot have 0 cholesterol — mainly a Switzerland/VA recording artifact) → set to missing, then imputed with the per-country median |
| 7 | `fbs` | int | Fasting blood sugar > 120 mg/dl | `0` = false, `1` = true | 9.8% | imputed with the per-country mode |
| 8 | `restecg` | int | Resting electrocardiographic results | `0` = normal, `1` = ST-T wave abnormality, `2` = probable/definite left ventricular hypertrophy | 0.2% | imputed with the per-country mode |
| 9 | `thalach` | float | Maximum heart rate achieved during exercise test | typically 60–220 | 6.0% | imputed with the per-country median |
| 10 | `exang` | int | Exercise-induced angina | `0` = no, `1` = yes | 6.0% | imputed with the per-country mode |
| 11 | `oldpeak` | float | ST depression induced by exercise relative to rest | ≥ 0, typically 0–6.2 | 6.7% + 12 illogical (negative values) | negative values treated as data-entry errors → set to missing, then imputed with the per-country median |
| 12 | `slope` | int | Slope of the peak exercise ST segment | `1` = upsloping, `2` = flat, `3` = downsloping | 33.6% | imputed with the per-country mode (below the 40% drop threshold, so kept) |
| 13 | `num` | int | Original diagnosis label — angiographic disease severity | `0` = no disease, `1`–`4` = increasing severity of disease presence | 0% | none needed |
| 14 | `target` | int | Simplified binary diagnosis label derived from `num` | `0` = no disease (`num == 0`), `1` = disease present (`num` > 0) | 0% (derived column) | none needed |

